m/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-29T17:56:29Z","updated_at":"2024-12-29T18:18:17Z","body":"@Rudolph-B can you say more on the issues with orthogonal cameras you pointed out in #97712 ?\n\nThere are different motivations for this PR that unintentionally brought me to propose reverting yours 😅. One of them is to not rely on Euclidean distance to support very large scenes. The other one is to get rid of specific code paths for orthogonal to prepare the support of custom projection matrices(https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11436).\n\nI'm wondering whether your abandoned solution 2 could actually solve both.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2564798834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565157815","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100907#issuecomment-2565157815","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100907","id":2565157815,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y5TO3","user":{"login":"Rudolph-B","id":52322745,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzIyNzQ1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52322745?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B","html_url":"https://github.com/Rudolph-B","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rudolph-B/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T08:18:38Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T08:19:04Z","body":"My comment in #97712, I don't think is relevant anymore. The were multitudes of problems with the orthogonal case that muddied the waters.\r\n\r\nThe only issue in moving back to depth space that I can see is what me and @lawnjelly discussed in those threads.\r\n> The one thing I'm slightly concerned is this may end up checking bounding box corners that are outside the view frustum, which may be closer to the camera plane than necessary and result in too small a `min_depth`, and thus unnecessarily rendering objects that could be rejected. I'm not sure on this, would be nice to have confirmed. I.e. ideally you maybe would intersect the AABB with the view frustum to find the closest point of the AABB _within_ view (or some equivalent technique).\r\n\r\nHaving played around a lot more with occlusion culling since then I am not really convinced that the situation for these  false negatives occur often (and even if they do it should be no more than a handful of object not thousands) enough to consider.  \r\n\r\nI am unable to test anything at the moment but I see sense in the advantages you listed. In that case updating and implementing  #97712 should solve both yes.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565157815/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565214439","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100907#issuecomment-2565214439","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100907","id":2565214439,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6Y5hDn","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-12-30T09:09:02Z","updated_at":"2024-12-30T09:13:55Z","body":"Thanks for following up, it's all clear.\n\nTook another look at #97712 and I believe it does the trick indeed.\n\nOn frustum clipping, it's not clear whether the added complexity would be balanced by the gain in false positives. I have to wrap my mind around how to step back to the closest in-frustum point on the AABB when the tested corner is outside, especially considering the AABB is not in view space.\n\nOne option I can think of is to reason with AABBs in clip space. But transforming a world-space AABB to clip space would enlarge it, which would introduce false positives...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2565214439/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2688227728","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100907#issuecomment-2688227728","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/100907","id":2688227728,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6gOxmQ","user":{"login":"Flarkk","id":49606622,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5NjA2NjIy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49606622?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk","html_url":"https://github.com/Flarkk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Flarkk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-02-27T15:03:55Z","updated_at":"2025-02-27T15:03:55Z","body":"Closing this one in favor of #97712 I'd suggest reopening.\r\nConsidering the above reflections, the edge case that motivated abandoning it is in my opinion not worth the overhead added by the chosen solution (that is to move the entire occlusion buffer to euclidian distance).","